---
/**
 * Mimics & Mythmakers, hung in the Gallery: an essay in six depths and one
 * ascent. The page is a water column. It opens on the surface (the feed,
 * Echo, the pick-me man), breaks the waterline ("So go in."), and sinks
 * through the five ocean zones, each opened by the Greek its name comes
 * from (epi, mesos, bathys, abyssos, Hades), to Challenger Deep, then
 * climbs back up (anabasis) to a gold dawn: "Act like it." A depth readout
 * and gauge track the meters; a fixed canvas carries light rays, bubbles,
 * marine snow and bioluminescence, and a tap in the dark makes light.
 * Unit charts for bioluminescence, men's friendships, screen hours,
 * reading and literacy; a dive-profile diagram; sources as Soundings.
 *
 * Ported from the owner's Claude artifact
 * (claude.ai/artifact/Uoi1YmTv8Apc8kKFsD6N5r); the essay text and its look
 * are the design of record. Its stylesheet is scoped under body.mimics so
 * Poem.astro's main, section and line globals cannot reach it.
 */
import Poem from '../../layouts/Poem.astro';
---

